      "asset_path": "figures/Genetics_A5.1.png",
      "caption": "Figure A5.1 Power (1−β) and significance (α) of a normally (left) and F-distributed test statistics (right). The distributions of the test statistic under the null hypothesis (H₀) and at a particular parameter value under the alternative hypothesis (H₁) are shown. Under the null hypothesis, the probability that the test statistic exceeds a critical value (Tₑ, Fₑ) is α, and we define this as the significance of the test. The power of the test for a particular value of the alternative hypothesis is the probability that the test statistic exceeds the critical value, and we denote this by 1 − β. Hence, β is the probability that the test statistic is below the critical value (a false negative).",
